From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] explorer: only top-level windows have taskbar buttons

A window created top-level and later made another window's child kept its taskbar button: comdlg32's file dialog creates its custom-controls pane top-level and puts it into the dialog, and Shotcut's Export dialog showed a second Shotcut button with an icon and no title. As on Windows, a button is shown only for a window whose parent is the desktop.
---
diff --git a/programs/explorer/systray.c b/programs/explorer/systray.c
index dd67f3f..271b927 100644
--- a/programs/explorer/systray.c
+++ b/programs/explorer/systray.c
@@ -1424,8 +1424,15 @@ static void sync_taskbar_buttons(void)
          * it asks for one with WS_EX_APPWINDOW */
         /* an elevated window is on another desktop, whose windows
          * IsWindowVisible calls hidden: its own style says */
+        /* Stained Glass OS (wine-sg 6098): and only a top-level window. A window created
+         * top-level and then put into another (the file dialog's custom controls pane, which
+         * comdlg32 makes a child of the dialog) kept its button: Shotcut's Export dialog
+         * had a second Shotcut button, an icon and no title */
         win->visible = win->xwin ? TRUE :
                        (win->elevated ? (GetWindowLongW( win->hwnd, GWL_STYLE ) & WS_VISIBLE) != 0 : IsWindowVisible( win->hwnd )) &&
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_CHILD_BUTTON
+                       (win->elevated || GetAncestor( win->hwnd, GA_PARENT ) == GetDesktopWindow()) &&
+#endif
                        !GetWindow( win->hwnd, GW_OWNER ) &&
                        ((GetWindowLongW( win->hwnd, GWL_EXSTYLE ) & (WS_EX_TOOLWINDOW | WS_EX_APPWINDOW)) != WS_EX_TOOLWINDOW) &&
                        (win->elevated || vd_on_current( win->hwnd ));
